  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$ and ${lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x)=8,$ then what is the value of $\\sqrt{f(-1)+1}?$",
  "worked_solution": "We're told that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1.$ According to the definition of continuity, this means that ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)$ exists, and\n\n$$\nf(-1)={lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x)=8.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{f(-1)+1} & =\\sqrt{8+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
